  VERDICT
==========================================================================================================================================
  cells: 20   positive total return: 16/20   beats underlying B&H on total return: 0/20   on Sharpe: 0/20
  mean 'theta drag' = -3% of all premium outlaid was lost to decay net of payoffs
  mean 44% of options expired worthless (100% loss, pure decay)
  SPY vs its B&H:  14/ATM -28% vs +677%; 14/OTM2 -87% vs +677%; 35/ATM +3% vs +677%; 35/OTM2 -39% vs +677%

  -> KILL. The defined-risk long-call structure does NOT pay off historically once BS-approximated premium,
     realistic option bid/ask, and time decay are charged. Time decay is the dominant loss channel; the
     capped downside does not compensate. Loses to simply holding the underlying on total return AND Sharpe.
     SPY/QQQ (near-real IV) results are trustworthy; AAPL/MSFT/GOOGL (RV proxy) are an optimistic upper bound
     and still lose -- so the kill is robust to the data limitation.

